    "body": "I'm surprised we don't say anything about the `option` element being disabled here.\n\nAlso, even if we fix this, I wonder if we need another issue to address this for appearance base:\n\n> If a [select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-select-element) element contains a [placeholder label option](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#placeholder-label-option), the user agent is [expected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#expected) to render that [option](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-option-element) in a manner that conveys that it is a label, rather than a valid option of the control. This can include preventing the [placeholder label option](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#placeholder-label-option) from being explicitly selected by the user. When the [placeholder label option](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#placeholder-label-option)'s [selectedness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#concept-option-selectedness) is true, the control is [expected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#expected) to be displayed in a fashion that indicates that no valid option is currently selected.\n",
